# Trusted signing keys, for `git verify-tag` over SSH signatures.
#
# Format: <email> <key-type> <public key>   — one per line, the public half only.
# A private key never appears here or anywhere else in this repository.
#
# One line per machine. The private half never leaves the machine that generated it, so a
# second machine gets its own key and its own line — which is why the key's title in
# GitHub names the machine, and why revoking one does not disturb the other.
#
# The release workflow refuses to run while this file holds no key. That check reads the
# file for a key line rather than grepping for a placeholder phrase: a check a comment can
# satisfy is not a check.

